note Alpha landing structure authored in Omega. Run with pinned hive-page omc.
text hero "<article class=\"alpha\"><header class=\"alpha-hero\"><p class=\"alpha-kicker\">SOVEREIGN INTELLIGENCE / BUILT ON AienOS</p><h1>Sovereign<br><span>Intelligence.</span></h1><p class=\"alpha-lead\">Alpha testing is open. Keep the GPU. Lose the user-space stack.</p><div class=\"alpha-install\"><code id=\"alpha-command\">git clone --branch alpha-20261026.2 https://github.com/aien-dev/sovereign-intelligence &amp;&amp; cd sovereign-intelligence &amp;&amp; sh installer/install.sh</code><button id=\"alpha-copy\" type=\"button\">Copy command</button></div><p id=\"alpha-copy-status\" class=\"alpha-copy-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"></p><p class=\"alpha-small\">Linux arm64 + NVIDIA GB10 only. Experimental software, installed beside your existing stack. Everything comes from the public GitHub repo <a href=\"https://github.com/aien-dev/sovereign-intelligence\">aien-dev/sovereign-intelligence</a>, so you can read it before you run it: <a href=\"https://github.com/aien-dev/sovereign-intelligence/blob/alpha-20261026.2/installer/install.sh\">read installer/install.sh first</a>. It downloads only this tag's signed release from GitHub and checks the signature and SHA-256 before it unpacks anything. Nothing is downloaded from this website.</p><p class=\"alpha-payoff\">Meet Aien on your own Spark.</p><p class=\"alpha-small\"><strong>Coming in the next update:</strong> Aien's black hole, glass panes, science tools and Omega, running locally. This release installs the engine and Omega wizard, not the Aien experience yet.</p><a class=\"alpha-scroll\" href=\"#alpha-next\">See what happens next ↓</a></header>\n"
text scene "<figure class=\"alpha-scene\" aria-labelledby=\"alpha-scene-caption\"><div class=\"alpha-space\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><svg class=\"alpha-orbits\" viewBox=\"0 0 1000 500\" fill=\"none\"><ellipse cx=\"500\" cy=\"250\" rx=\"445\" ry=\"125\"/><ellipse cx=\"500\" cy=\"250\" rx=\"360\" ry=\"95\"/><ellipse cx=\"500\" cy=\"250\" rx=\"270\" ry=\"65\"/><path d=\"M35 110 Q500 480 965 110 M35 390 Q500 20 965 390\"/></svg><div class=\"alpha-disc\"></div><div class=\"alpha-hole\"></div><div class=\"alpha-infall\"><span data-stack=\"0\">CUDA toolkit</span><span data-stack=\"1\">libcuda</span><span data-stack=\"2\">cuBLAS</span><span data-stack=\"3\">nvcc</span></div><div class=\"alpha-kept\"><span>YOUR GPU / STAYS</span><span>KERNEL DRIVER / STAYS</span></div></div><figcaption id=\"alpha-scene-caption\"><strong>The event horizon is a metaphor.</strong> I am cutting the NVIDIA user-space dependency out of my inference path, not deleting your CUDA packages. Your GPU and NVIDIA kernel driver stay.</figcaption><button class=\"alpha-motion\" id=\"alpha-motion\" type=\"button\" aria-pressed=\"false\">Play the event horizon</button></figure>\n"
text next "<section class=\"alpha-section\" id=\"alpha-next\"><p class=\"alpha-kicker\">01 / THE ARRIVAL</p><h2>One download. Then a walkthrough.</h2><ol class=\"alpha-steps\"><li><span>DOWNLOAD</span><h3>Clone it from GitHub.</h3><p>git fetches the installer's readable source from the public repo. install.sh checks your machine, downloads the signed bundle from GitHub Releases, verifies it, then adds a launcher at user level.</p></li><li><span>DOUBLE-CLICK</span><h3>Open the launcher.</h3><p>Open Sovereign Intelligence from your applications menu. The terminal wizard shows what it will change before asking for consent.</p></li><li><span>WIZARD</span><h3>Make the first run yours.</h3><p>Doctor, plan, consent, install, model download, first chat. The wizard names the download and its size before you agree.</p></li></ol><div class=\"alpha-capture\"><p class=\"alpha-terminal-bar\">SOVEREIGN INTELLIGENCE / OMEGA TERMINAL WIZARD</p><img src=\"/alpha/wizard-plan.svg\" width=\"900\" height=\"612\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"Captured Omega wizard plan screen: the side-by-side release and model paths, with NVIDIA packages left untouched.\"><details><summary>Read the captured terminal text</summary>"
text support "</details></div><p class=\"alpha-small\">Captured from the real Omega wizard in a fake-root host run. This is not a GPU installation receipt.</p></section><section class=\"alpha-section\" id=\"alpha-hardware\"><p class=\"alpha-kicker\">02 / KNOW THE BOUNDARY</p><h2>One machine family first.</h2><div class=\"alpha-columns\"><div><h3>NVIDIA DGX Spark / GB10</h3><p>The install target is Linux arm64 with an NVIDIA GB10 (PCI 10de:2e12) and NVIDIA kernel driver 580.173.02. The doctor refuses machines with less than 64 GiB of memory and warns when the GB10 has less than 61,309 MiB free. I am not offering a Windows, macOS, x86 Linux or other-GPU installer yet. Unsupported machines receive a friendly “not yet” without an installation.</p><p>The model is <strong>Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-FP8</strong>, pinned to revision <code>95a723d0</code>: 37,493,015,668 bytes in 56 files, each hash-checked. The plan asks for that size plus 1 GB of free disk. A 27B option is still to come and is not offered in this release.</p><h3>What is coming for other machines?</h3><p><strong>PROPOSED:</strong> more hardware and operating systems, after a working port and device-specific evidence. I will not label a machine supported because the code compiles. <a href=\"https://github.com/aien-dev/omega-projects/issues\">Tell me which machine you want to test</a>.</p></div><aside class=\"alpha-evidence\"><p class=\"alpha-kicker\">EVIDENCE, NOT A PROMISE</p><h3>Alpha is a testing phase.</h3><p><strong>EXERCISED:</strong> the bundled engine <code>19173f9e</code> is byte for byte the build serving this 35B on my Spark, and I rebuilt it byte-identically from Core commit <code>59b05a71</code>. That is a development build, not a Core release tag.</p><p><strong>EXERCISED:</strong> installer, wizard and uninstaller on a fake GB10 tree (33/33), plus a stock Ubuntu 24.04 arm64 container (6/6 with a negative control). The first chat ran only against a fake engine.</p><p><strong>NOT_RUN:</strong> a real GB10 install from this installer, its 37.5 GB download and first token, and three-pass physical qualification. I am not calling this installer hardware-qualified.</p><p><a href=\"https://github.com/aien-dev/sovereign-intelligence/releases/tag/alpha-20261026.2\">Release, exact artifacts and evidence</a></p></aside></div><p class=\"alpha-small\"><a href=\"https://github.com/aien-dev/sovereign-intelligence\">Sovereign Intelligence is the front door</a>. AienOS is its OS layer; Aien, Omega, aien-math and CUDA++ keep their own identities. <a href=\"https://github.com/aien-dev/sovereign-intelligence/blob/main/docs/WHAT-I-AM-BUILDING.md\">Read my project audit</a>.</p></section>\n"
text source "<section class=\"alpha-section\" id=\"alpha-source\"><p class=\"alpha-kicker\">03 / NOTHING HIDDEN</p><h2>Built entirely in Omega.</h2><p class=\"alpha-lead\">The walkthrough wizard is a seeded <code>.om</code> program. This page's structure and small motion client are generated by Omega too. Read the source, keep a copy, change it.</p><p>I mean the wizard, not every dependency in the delivery chain: the download bootstrap is POSIX sh, the website builder is Rust, and the host still supplies Linux, a terminal, signature verification and the NVIDIA kernel driver. Those boundaries are explicit.</p><p>The wizard source below targets seeded Omega compiler revision <code>3364a1dfd</code>. This page generator uses its separately pinned compiler; they are not interchangeable.</p><div class=\"alpha-links\"><a href=\"https://github.com/aien-dev/sovereign-intelligence/tree/alpha-20261026.2/installer/wizard\">Browse the wizard source</a><a href=\"https://github.com/aien-dev/sovereign-intelligence/releases/download/alpha-20261026.2/aienos.om\">Get aienos.om from the GitHub release ↓</a><a href=\"https://github.com/aien-dev/aienos.com/tree/main/om/alpha-page\">Read this page's Omega</a></div><p class=\"alpha-small\">aienos.om is the wizard as one plain-text file, SHA-256 <code>d7459752ee454aab116b60c7e5fa7ad7e7a591c2fc52342ea0483590ea91b120</code>, listed in the release's signed SHA256SUMS.</p><details class=\"alpha-source\"><summary>Read the wizard's .om source</summary><pre><code>"
text finish "</code></pre></details></section><section class=\"alpha-section\" id=\"alpha-feedback\"><p class=\"alpha-kicker\">04 / BUILD IT WITH ME</p><h2>Tell me what happened.</h2><p><a href=\"https://github.com/aien-dev/omega-projects/issues\">Open an issue in omega-projects</a>. Include your hardware, operating system, release tag, the step that failed and the exact error. Remove tokens, personal paths, private prompts and model data before sharing a log.</p></section><section class=\"alpha-section alpha-exit\" id=\"alpha-uninstall\"><p class=\"alpha-kicker\">05 / THE WAY BACK</p><h2>No one-way door.</h2><p>The installation lives under <code>~/.local/share/aienos</code>. It does not uninstall or overwrite NVIDIA packages or CUDA. Run <code>aienos uninstall</code> and type <code>yes</code> when asked. It removes the alpha installation, downloaded model, command and launchers. To keep the downloaded model, use <code>aienos uninstall --keep-model</code>. If the command is missing, run <code>~/.local/share/aienos/current/bin/aienos uninstall</code>.</p>"
text amp "&amp;"
text less "&lt;"
text more "&gt;"
text pre "<pre>"
text endpre "</pre>"
text ending "<p><a href=\"https://github.com/aien-dev/sovereign-intelligence\">Uninstaller source and release instructions</a></p><p class=\"alpha-small\">I would rather hear why you left than make it difficult to leave.</p></section></article>"
fn emit s view uchar 65536 n ulong to int
pos = ulong 0
start = ulong 0
while lt pos n bound 65536
b = get s pos
if or eq b 38 or eq b 60 eq b 62
if gt pos start
k = write 1 s start sub pos start
if ne k long sub pos start
ret 1
end
end
if eq b 38
k = write 1 amp 0 len amp
if ne k long len amp
ret 1
end
else
if eq b 60
k = write 1 less 0 len less
if ne k long len less
ret 1
end
else
k = write 1 more 0 len more
if ne k long len more
ret 1
end
end
end
start = add pos 1
end
pos = add pos 1
end
if gt n start
k = write 1 s start sub n start
if ne k long sub n start
ret 1
end
end
ret 0
end
fn include fd int to int
buf = new uchar 65536 0
total = ulong 0
while true bound 65536
n = read fd buf 0 len buf
if lt n 0
ret 2
end
if eq n 0
if eq total 0
ret 3
end
ret 0
end
total = add total ulong n
if gt total 1048576
ret 4
end
r = emit buf ulong n
if ne r 0
ret r
end
end
ret 5
end
fn main to int
w = write 1 hero 0 len hero
if ne w long len hero
ret 1
end
w = write 1 scene 0 len scene
if ne w long len scene
ret 1
end
w = write 1 next 0 len next
if ne w long len next
ret 1
end
w = write 1 pre 0 len pre
if ne w long len pre
ret 1
end
r = include 4
if ne r 0
ret r
end
w = write 1 endpre 0 len endpre
if ne w long len endpre
ret 1
end
w = write 1 support 0 len support
if ne w long len support
ret 1
end
w = write 1 source 0 len source
if ne w long len source
ret 1
end
r = include 5
if ne r 0
ret r
end
w = write 1 finish 0 len finish
if ne w long len finish
ret 1
end
w = write 1 ending 0 len ending
if ne w long len ending
ret 1
end
ret 0
end
